.TH makekey 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
makekey \- turn a key into an encryption key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B makekey
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B makekey
reads ten bytes from standard input and writes thirteen: eight bytes of
key and two of salt, turned into a value for
.BR crypt (1)
to use.  The transformation is deliberately slow.
.PP
It is not run by hand.  It exists for
.BR crypt (1)
and for the editors that once encrypted files.
.SH NOTES
The algorithm behind this dates from the 1970s and is not a means of
keeping anything secret from anyone who is trying.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crypt (1),
.BR passwd (1)
